              "text": "1. Anomalies in One Wide Table",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Insert}: can't add a course without a student",
                "{orange:Update}: change many rows, miss some",
                "{purple:Delete}: removing the last student loses the course"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Normal Forms",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Rule"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "1NF",
                  "==Atomic== cells, row identified by a key"
                ],
                [
                  "2NF",
                  "1NF + no ==partial== dependency"
                ],
                [
                  "3NF",
                  "2NF + no ==transitive==; X super key or Y prime"
                ],
                [
                  "BCNF",
                  "Every nontrivial X→Y: X is a ==super key=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "2NF only matters for **composite** keys",
                "BCNF is stricter; can lose ==dependency preservation=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Decompose",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
